<title>USA: Intermet to buy 49 pct of machining firm.</title>
<headline>Intermet to buy 49 pct of machining firm.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intermet Corp said on Monday it agreed to acquire 49 percent of IWESA GmbH, a precision machining and engineering company based in Saarbrucken, Germany, effective November 1.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>&quot;Our goal in pursuing this joint venture is to expand our presence in Europe and to take advantage of a significant new market opportunity,&quot; said Intermet chairman John Doddridge in a statement.</p>
<p>IWESA had sales of $21 million and assets of $17 million for the fiscal year ended December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
